Today I solved leetcode question 2300: Successfull Pairs of Spells and Potions.

Description: We are given two arrays named spells and potion. And an integer named success.
              A spell and a potion pair is considered successfull if their product is greater than or equal to success.
              We must return an array of answers where each index represents total number of successful pairs a spell can make.
              eg- spells=[1,2,3] potions=[1,2,3,4,5] success=5
                  ans=[2,3,4]

Solution: If we use double for loop to check each and every paie we will get TLE.
          So here we first sort the potions array and then check the first index where the potion and spell pair is successful.
          And every element after that will form a successful pair.
          First we create an answer pair.
          Then we sort the potions array.
          Then we will start a for loop of same size of spells array.
          Inside for loop we will assign 2 values one low and another high.
          Low being 0 and high being size of potions array minus 1.
          And we will create a index variable and assign it the value -1.
          Then we will start a while loop till low is less than equal to high.
          Then we will create a variable named midd inside while loop.
          It will be sum of high and low and then divided by 2.
          Then we will check whether element at index midd is forminig successful pair with the current spells index.
          If yes we will assign answer the value of midd. And we will assign the high as midd minus 1.
          Else we will make low as midd plus 1.
          If our index variable is still -1 then we will add 0 to our answer array. And if not then we will just add size minus index to our answer array.
